x^46655 ≡ 5 (mod 9)

We can start by noticing that any number modulo 9 can be represented as the sum of its digits. This is known as "casting out nines".

Using this property, we can rewrite x as the sum of its digits, i.e:
x = n1 + n2 + n3 +... + nk

Then:
x^46655 ≡ (n1 + n2 + n3 +... + nk)^46655 (mod 9)

