[Step 280] Q: Given real numbers $x$ and $y$ satisfy $|x-2|+\left(y+3\right)^{2}=0$, then the value of the algebraic expression $\left(x+y\right)^{2023}$ is ______.
Ground truth: -1
Response[0]:
<start_working_out>

We are given that $|x-2|+\left(y+3\right)^{2}=0$. 

Since the absolute value of any number is always non-negative, the only way the sum of the absolute value and the square of any number can be zero is if both terms are individually zero.

Therefore, $|x-2|=0$ and $\left(y+3\right)^{2}=0$. 

This means that $x-2=0$ and $y+3=0$, which in turn implies that $x=2$ and $y=-3$.

Fin
