[Step 460] Q: I bought 16 pencils at a stationery store, but I lost a few on the way back home. When I counted the number of remaining pencils, there were 8. How many pencils were lost?
Ground truth: 8
Response[0]:
<start_working_out>
To find out how many pencils were lost, we need to subtract the number of remaining pencils from the number of pencils I initially bought.
I initially bought 16 pencils.
I have 8 pencils remaining.

Number of pencils lost = Initial pencils - Remaining pencils
= 16 - 8
= 8

<end_working_out>
<SOLUTION>8</SOLUTION>
