[Step 860] Q: I have 150 pieces of cake. There are some friends in my house. I would like to give each friend the same amount of cake, which is 3 pieces per friend. How many friends are in my house?
Ground truth: 50
Response[0]:
<start_working_out>
To find the number of friends, we need to divide the total amount of cake (150) by the amount of cake each friend will get (3).

Number of friends = Total cake / Cake per friend
= 150 / 3
= 50

So, there are 50 friends in the house.

<end_working_out>
